WEBVTT

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.240
Every AI conversation has a price.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.380
Almost none of them will tell you what it is.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.950
So we made a receipt you hand to the conversation itself.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.050
It's a short instruction. You can read every line before you copy it.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.640
Paste it after any chat in ChatGPT or Claude.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.490
The assistant counts the messages you can see, estimates the tokens,

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:37.530
and checks PromptSpend's current prices, live.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:41.570
Then it tells you the cost range, and the two things driving it.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:47.825
And it says what it can't see. Hidden prompts. Tool calls. Cached context.

00:00:47.875 --> 00:00:52.800
It says "estimate," never "invoice."

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:57.820
If it can't check a price, it says so, instead of guessing.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.655
Then turn the answer into a receipt you can share.

00:01:01.705 --> 00:01:04.360
Made on your machine, not ours.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:09.080
Your prompt has a price tag. PromptSpend it.
